FWIW, in real life, lava tends to solidify after coming into contact
with a cold object (cold relative to the lava---which is almost
everything). E.g., lava flowing around a tree will vaporize the wood,
but will at the same time form a cast of rock around where the wood used
to be (even the woodgrain is preserved! search the US Geological Survey
photographs sometime).

So, one could rationalize this "bug" as the boots vaporising, but
leaving a cast of rock where they used to be. As soon as you attempt to
step off them, you sink into the molten parts of the lava. (Of course,
IRL this has other unrealistic consequences, but we'll ignore those for
now.)


